240
00:10:58,250 --> 00:11:01,490
If I do a good job here,
then all of you will all

241
00:11:01,490 --> 00:11:03,350
there is to about
video generation.

242
00:11:03,350 --> 00:11:08,390
I'm imagining most of you
have more of a NLP background

243
00:11:08,390 --> 00:11:11,190
with text autoregressive models.

244
00:11:11,190 --> 00:11:12,800
I'm going to try
and contextualize

245
00:11:12,800 --> 00:11:16,580
all of this in relation to
text, and how it differs

246
00:11:16,580 --> 00:11:18,430
from large language models.

247
00:11:18,430 --> 00:11:22,200

248
00:11:22,200 --> 00:11:24,440
So the representation.

249
00:11:24,440 --> 00:11:25,710
What do we mean by that?

250
00:11:25,710 --> 00:11:27,543
Well, we mean, how are
we going to represent

251
00:11:27,543 --> 00:11:29,460
the data for the model?

252
00:11:29,460 --> 00:11:31,200
We're doing generative
